{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a000000000000001","type":"text","x":200,"y":-820,"width":5000,"height":600,"color":"5","text":"## Quality vs Valuation Scatter\n\nEvery active thesis plotted on **(quality × valuation)**. Y-axis = quality composite (ROIC, FCF margin, margin durability, growth quality, balance sheet). X-axis = valuation composite (forward multiple, **absolute across all sectors**, 0=very cheap, 100=very expensive).\n\n**Quadrants** (split at 50/50):\n- 🟢 **BARGAIN COMPOUNDER** (top-left): high quality + cheap → the holy grail. Rare in 2026 — quality has been bid up across the market.\n- 🔵 **PAYING UP FOR QUALITY** (top-right): high quality + expensive → acceptable if growth durability is real; vulnerable to multiple compression if growth softens.\n- 🟡 **VALUE TRAP RISK** (bottom-left): low quality + cheap → either deep value (asset/cycle thesis) or value trap. Diligence required.\n- 🔴 **DANGER ZONE** (bottom-right): low quality + expensive → story stocks; thesis depends on narrative-to-quality transition. Highest risk of permanent capital loss.\n\n**★ Inner zones**:\n- **Bargain Apex** (top-left corner, Q≥65 AND V≤50): the actual bargain compounder candidates. Cheaper than market with above-average quality.\n- **Premium Compounder** (upper-right corner, Q≥80 AND V≥65): elite-quality businesses justifying premium multiples. Acceptable holdings even at high P/E.\n- **Danger Apex** (bottom-right corner, Q≤40 AND V≥70): exit-or-justify candidates. Story stocks with no quality anchor.\n\n**Color = conviction**: green = HIGH · yellow = MEDIUM · red = LOW. **Excluded**: BTC, GLD (commodity exposure — no traditional Q/V framework).\n\n**Caveat**: valuation is absolute, not sector-relative. Software clusters right (expensive), Asian/cyclical equities cluster left (cheap) by design — this surfaces cross-sector relative-value opportunities."},
		{"id":"b000000000000001","type":"group","x":160,"y":160,"width":2540,"height":2040,"label":"BARGAIN COMPOUNDER — high quality + cheap","color":"4"},
