		{"id":"a000000000000050","type":"text","x":5400,"y":200,"width":1400,"height":3200,"color":"5","text":"## Portfolio Distribution\n\n**Bargain Apex** (1/58 = 1%):\nLNG\n\n**Bargain Compounder** (5/58 = 8%):\n000660, 6981, RELIANCE, EINK, SKM\n\n**Premium Compounder** (9/58 = 15%):\nKLA, LRCX, ASMI, NVDA, AVGO, NOW, INTU, APP, ISRG\n\n**Paying for Quality** (33/58 = 56%):\nAMAT, BESI, AIXA, FORM, AEHR, TSM, AMD, MRVL, 2802, PLTR, CRWD, PANW, NET, SHOP, WTC, CSGP, META, NFLX, SPOT, DUOL, TTWO, PINS, GAW, UBER, CRCL, VRT, VICR, DE, IOT, CCJ, LITE, PSTG, KAMBI\n\n**Value Trap Risk** (5/58 = 8%):\nINTC, 285A, SNDK, EDEL, STNG\n\n**Danger Zone** (4/58 = 6%):\nIQE, HIMS, MTN, OPEN\n\n**Danger Apex** (1/58 = 1%):\nCRWV\n\n---\n\n## Reads\n\n- **Bargain Apex** (1) — actively cheap quality. Rare; protect aggressively.\n- **Premium Compounder** (9) — premium-but-earned. Acceptable holds even at high multiples.\n- **Paying for Quality** (33) — bulk of portfolio. Multiples vulnerable to growth softening.\n- **Value Trap Risk + Danger** (10) — each needs explicit non-quality justification.\n\n**Within Paying for Quality**: scan for relative-value within similar-quality cohorts (e.g., AMAT 31x vs LRCX 48x in semicap)."}
